The two-point generator has neighbourhoods {0} and {0, Λ}, with master {0, Λ}, where 0 is the one-bit string false and Λ is the empty string. As a domain this is the chain with the singleton of 0 strictly below the master. The singleton sits inside the master, so the intersection of any two neighbourhoods is one of them, both neighbourhoods lie under the master, and both are nonempty.
